data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Dispatch d002 — implement greet, tested\\n\\n## What I did\\n\\nIn `~/subject` on branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`:\\n\\n1. Created `src/greet.py`:\\n\\n   ```python\\n   def greet(name):\\n       return \\\"Hello, {}!\\\".format(name)\\n   ```\\n\\n2. Created `tests/test_greet.py` with unittest cases for a normal name\\n   (`greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`) and the empty string\\n   (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`). The test file inserts `../src` onto\\n   `sys.path` so `greet` can be imported without adding any package\\n   `__init__.py` files (none were needed for `unittest discover` to find\\n   the test module itself).\\n\\n3. Ran the test suite exactly as specified:\\n\\n   ```\\n   $ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n   ..\\n   ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n   Ran 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\n   OK\\n   $ echo $?\\n   0\\n   ```\\n\\n   Both tests passed; exit code was 0. Nothing needed fixing.\\n\\n4. Committed the two new files to my own branch (no history rewrite):\\n\\n   ```\\n   [cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1> 89392e6] Add greet function with unit tests\\n    2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)\\n    create mode 100644 src/greet.py\\n    create mode 100644 tests/test_greet.py\\n   ```\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nOnly `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py` were added. No other files were\\ntouched or created (verified via `git status` before commit — only\\n`__pycache__/` directories were untracked, and those were not added).\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nTask complete. All requested tests pass, changes are committed to my branch.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

